# Long video (~15 min): why phone/internet "addiction" is profitable — the attention economy.
# Sources (checked):
#  - Meta 10-K FY2023: revenue $134.9B, advertising $131.9B (~98%). Alphabet 2023: Google advertising ≈ $237.9B of
#    $307.4B (~77%) (aggregators citing filings).
#  - DataReportal Digital 2024: ~6 h 40 min online per day; ~143 min/day on social media; 720 billion minutes/day total.
#  - Herbert Simon, "Designing Organizations for an Information-Rich World" (1971): "a wealth of information creates a
#    poverty of attention".
#  - Reed Hastings, Netflix Q1 2017 call (Apr 2017): "we're competing with sleep" (Fast Company, CNBC, NPR).
#  - Sean Parker, Axios event Nov 2017: "exploiting a vulnerability in human psychology", "a little dopamine hit",
#    "How do we consume as much of your time and conscious attention as possible?", "God only knows what it's doing to
#    our children's brains" (Axios, CBS, Fortune).
#  - Chamath Palihapitiya, Stanford GSB Nov 2017: "short-term, dopamine-driven feedback loops ... are destroying how
#    society works"; "tremendous guilt" (Axios, Fortune, Salon).
#  - Justin Rosenstein (co-creator of the Like button): The Guardian, Oct 2017 "Our minds can be hijacked".
#  - Aza Raskin invented infinite scroll (2006) and has said he regrets how it is used (NPR, Masters of Scale).
#  - Tristan Harris (ex-Google design ethicist) told the US Senate (2019) the pull-to-refresh/feeds work like a slot
#    machine; variable rewards: B. F. Skinner's experiments; Nir Eyal "Hooked" (2014), later "Indistractable" (2019).
#  - Cambridge Analytica: Facebook estimate up to 87 million users (Apr 2018); FTC $5B penalty (2019).
#  - Frances Haugen (Oct 2021): Instagram internal slide — 32% of teen girls said when they felt bad about their bodies,
#    Instagram made them feel worse; Meta disputed the interpretation.
#  - Oct 2023: 41 US states + DC sued Meta over addictive design harming youth (PBS, EdWeek).
#  - US Surgeon General advisory on social media and youth mental health (May 2023).
#  - Australia: law banning social media accounts for under-16s passed 28 Nov 2024 (NPR, Al Jazeera).
#  - WHO: "gaming disorder" in ICD-11 (adopted 2019); "smartphone addiction" is not a formal diagnosis.
#  - Brady et al., PNAS 2017: moral-emotional words increased retweet rates (≈20% per word) — told as "по одному исследованию".
#  - Apple Screen Time and Google Digital Wellbeing launched 2018.

def S(bg, *people, z=None, **kw):
    """shot: people = (who, pose) pairs; auto-places 1–3 characters and picks a camera."""
    xs = {0: [], 1: [540], 2: [330, 750], 3: [280, 540, 800]}[len(people)]
    zoom = z or (1.3 if len(people) <= 1 else 1.1)
    return dict(bg=bg, cast=[(w, x, p) for (w, p), x in zip(people, xs)], cam=(zoom, 540, 1050 if zoom < 1.6 else 930), **kw)
def P(who, expr="neutral", **pose): return (who, dict(expr=expr, **pose))
U, V, T, C, D, A = "user", "user2", "teen", "ceo", "designer", "adman"
PH = dict(arm_r=60)          # pose that holds a phone (use with fx="phone")

